From 827994aab2b4136b0b2f7de973e9d6b07919c145 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: well0nez <8986239+well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 02:25:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 08/30] allwinner: h713: PSCI SYSTEM_SUSPEND through the ARISC
 (plan 104 H1)

FB-STANDBY tfa-0001 (27.09.2026), rebased by crust-20261007 onto 4c1bd8c6 after
tfa-0002 (one hunk of platform.mk by hand: the sources list carries a comment
block behind it on this branch).

The native PSCI ops offered no SYSTEM_SUSPEND, so Linux could not even ask.
Now the H713 platform provides sunxi_system_suspend_enter(): one "cpu op req"
(type 0x22, attr 0, five words {mpidr, warm entry, 3, 3, 3}) on msgbox user1
port 3, the frame the vendor monitor builds at 0x66b4 and sends at 0x60a0. The
firmware takes the SoC down from there and releases CPU0 at the warm entry it
was given. The common code gains get_sys_suspend_power_state, the system-level
branch in suspend and suspend_finish (GIC distributor re-init, platform hook)
and keeps the warm entry point in sunxi_sec_entrypoint. A request that cannot
be delivered resets the board instead of sleeping with nothing to wake it.
All of it sits behind SUNXI_SYSTEM_SUSPEND, which only the H713 platform sets.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
